{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"P2 (Gerrit 2459) PS5 pushed (rev 98cca52c). Convergence-matrix audit round: fixed the BLOCKING forced/dedup-disabled observability gap — a force=True or REBAR_MCP_DEDUP=0 async start now registers a standalone singleflight entry (key 'standalone\\0<job_id>', NUL-guarded so it never collides with content sha256 keys) so is_job_active(job_id) is True for the daemon lifetime and complete() purges it. Also: follower start now resolves gate_status -> 'attaching' (rec None but is_job_active True) instead of a missing-entry 'unknown'; _durable_verdict now always returns an explicit {ok:False,verdict:'unknown',reason:...} dict on exception instead of silently dropping 'durable'. 6 new matrix tests (forced/dedup ×3, attaching, durable-on-exception, unknown-stays-unknown); RED->GREEN teeth verified per fix. Full {leader,follower,forced,dedup-disabled}×{observable-active,gate_status-sane,is_job_active,no-clobber} matrix now holds. make lint + make typecheck green; mcp-reference no drift. Not submitting/closing."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788159060566511001,"uuid":"a86eed44-b7b9-4bd1-abdd-abf13a8ee45f"}